## 7. Database Design

### Entity list (summary — see PRD §10 for descriptions)
User, Target, JobRequirement, Skill, UserSkill, Evidence, Project, ProjectSkill, Roadmap, RoadmapItem, GitHubRepository, Assessment.

### Key relationships
- `User` 1—N `Target`
- `Target` 1—N `JobRequirement` (each referencing one `Skill`)
- `User` 1—N `UserSkill` (each referencing one `Skill`)
- `User` 1—N `Evidence` (each referencing one `Skill`, optionally one `GitHubRepository` or `Project`)
- `User` 1—N `Project`; `Project` N—N `Skill` via `ProjectSkill`
- `Target` 1—1..N `Roadmap`; `Roadmap` 1—N `RoadmapItem` (each referencing one `Skill`, optionally one `Project`)
- `User` 1—N `GitHubRepository`
- `User` 1—N `Assessment` (each referencing one `Skill`)

### Important fields, indexes, constraints
- `Skill.name` — unique; `Skill.aliases` — text array or join table for normalization lookups; index on `Skill.category`.
- `UserSkill(userId, skillId)` — unique composite constraint (one entry per user per skill; confidence/source updated in place).
- `Evidence(userId, skillId)` — indexed (not unique — multiple evidence items per skill are expected); index on `sourceType` for filtering.
- `JobRequirement(targetId, skillId)` — unique composite constraint.
- `RoadmapItem(roadmapId, skillId)` — indexed; `status` indexed for dashboard filtering.
- `GitHubRepository(userId, githubId)` — unique composite constraint; index on `lastSyncedAt` for scheduling next sync.
- All foreign keys `ON DELETE CASCADE` from `User` where appropriate (e.g., deleting a user cascades Targets, UserSkills, Evidence) to satisfy the "delete my data" privacy requirement; `Target` deletion cascades `JobRequirement`, `Roadmap`, `RoadmapItem` (soft-delete first, hard-delete after retention window per PRD §13).

