## 10. AI Architecture

> **MVP scoring boundaries:** Evidence Level 0–5 is computed internally and stored for deterministic gap/scoring logic, but the detailed 0–5 scale does not need to be surfaced in the MVP UI. Portfolio Strength is a deterministic/basic signal score in MVP; the deeper Portfolio Quality Audit is post-MVP. Assessment records are reserved for post-MVP verification/Interview Mode and are unused in MVP.



- **Model/provider:** Anthropic Claude API (or any OpenAI-compatible provider) — abstracted behind a single internal `AIProvider` interface (`extractJobRequirements`, `extractResumeProfile`, `generateRoadmap`, `generateProjectIdeas`, `critiqueResumeClaim`) so the concrete provider can be swapped without touching business logic.
- **Prompt architecture:** Each AI capability has a **versioned prompt template** stored in code (not user-editable), paired with a **strict JSON output schema** (validated with Zod on receipt). Prompts instruct the model to only extract/infer from the given input and never invent skills, employers, or evidence not present in the source text.
- **Context management:** Each AI call is stateless and single-purpose (no long conversational memory needed); all required context (job description text, resume text, current skill list) is passed explicitly in the prompt per call.
- **Memory:** No persistent AI "memory" across sessions — SkillGap's own database is the source of truth for user state; the AI is used as a stateless extraction/generation tool, not an agent with memory. This is a deliberate simplicity/trust choice.
- **Retrieval/RAG:** Not required for MVP — job descriptions and resumes are short enough to fit directly in a single prompt context window. (Flagged as a future enhancement if job description history/market-trend features are built post-MVP.)
- **Token/cost considerations:** Cache AI results by content hash (e.g., hash of job description text) to avoid re-processing identical input; cap input length (truncate extremely long job descriptions/resumes with a user-facing notice); batch skill normalization where possible.
- **Failure handling:** On malformed JSON or schema-validation failure, retry once with a stricter "return only valid JSON" instruction; on repeated failure, fall back to a deterministic template (e.g., keyword-based skill matching against the `Skill` table) and flag the result as "basic analysis — AI unavailable."
- **Safety considerations:** Never send GitHub access tokens or full file contents beyond what's needed (e.g., README text, file listing) to the AI provider; strip any obviously sensitive resume fields (e.g., government ID numbers) before sending resume text to the LLM, if detected.

