## 14. Logging, Monitoring & Error Tracking

- Structured JSON logs for: AI calls (capability, prompt version, latency, token usage if available, success/failure), GitHub sync jobs (repo count, duration, rate-limit status), and all API errors.
- Frontend and backend error tracking via a free-tier error tracking service (e.g., Sentry), capturing unhandled exceptions with user id (pseudonymous) and request context, excluding sensitive payload contents (resume text, job descriptions) from error reports.
- Background job status table (`jobId, type, status, startedAt, completedAt, error`) doubles as both a monitoring surface and the polling mechanism for the frontend.
- Basic uptime/latency monitoring via the hosting platform's built-in analytics for MVP; a dedicated APM tool is a post-MVP enhancement.

