## 15. Deployment Architecture

- **Development:** Local Next.js dev server + local or cloud dev Postgres instance (e.g., a free Neon branch); `.env.local` for secrets; Prisma migrations run locally against the dev DB.
- **Staging:** A separate Vercel preview environment (automatic per-PR previews) pointed at a separate Neon/Supabase branch database, used for manual QA before merging to `main`.
- **Production:** Vercel production deployment triggered on merge to `main`; production Postgres instance (Neon/Supabase); environment variables/secrets configured in the Vercel dashboard (never in source control).
- Database migrations run as an explicit deployment step (`prisma migrate deploy`) before/at the start of the production deploy, not automatically on every cold start.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    DEV[Local Dev] -->|git push| GH[GitHub Repo]
    GH -->|PR| PREVIEW[Vercel Preview + Staging DB]
    GH -->|merge to main| PROD[Vercel Production]
    PROD --> PRODDB[(Production Postgres)]
    PREVIEW --> STAGEDB[(Staging Postgres)]
```

