## 17. Architectural Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| Modular monolith over microservices | Small team, tightly related domain entities, faster to build/deploy/debug. |
| Deterministic code for gap-status and scoring, AI only for extraction/generation | Reduces hallucination risk and keeps scores explainable/reproducible (source spec §27, §30). |
| Background job table instead of Redis queue for MVP | Avoids an extra infra dependency; clear, low-risk upgrade path if needed. |
| AI provider behind an internal interface | Keeps the system provider-agnostic and testable (can mock the interface in tests). |
| Resume/GitHub extraction requires user confirmation before being saved as fact | Prevents hallucinated or misdetected data from silently corrupting the user's profile and trust in the product. |
| Row-level ownership checks in the repository layer, not just at the route layer | Defense in depth against IDOR-style access bugs. |
| GitHub evidence explicitly labeled "detected, not verified mastery" | Matches source spec's explicit requirement that GitHub detection is evidence, not proof (source spec §11). |

